I’m not sure I understand the question, or what I might say beyond what I said in the previous response <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/T661FsAdIv4/m/75GrqSl8AQAJ>: “The question of what to do with non-normal phenotype distributions in QTL mapping is the same as the question of what to do with non-normally distributed outcomes in multiple linear regression. Generally linear regression is quite robust, and non-constant residual variance is a bigger problem than non-normality.”

karl

